From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Schultz <alexschultz002@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:25:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: spell: spell_cmp must return int for qsort (64bit made
 it s64)

64bit.sh's '(\<int\> )' -> 's64 ' rewrite turned the qsort comparator's return type into s64; qsort requires int (*)(const void *, const void *), and GCC 14 rejects the incompatible pointer. Only the return type is changed back.
---
 ex.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ex.c b/ex.c
index 979cd0b5..0e8766ea 100644
--- a/ex.c
+++ b/ex.c
@@ -1502,7 +1502,7 @@ static char *spcmd;		/* the speller in use */
 static char spmsg[128];		/* the speller's own complaint, forwarded */
 
 /* speller lines by word, "& word cnt off: sug, sug" and "# word off" */
-static s64 spell_cmp(const void *v1, const void *v2)
+static int spell_cmp(const void *v1, const void *v2)
 {
 	char *s1 = *(char *const *)v1 + 2, *s2 = *(char *const *)v2 + 2;
 	for (; *s1 == *s2 && *s1 && *s1 != ' '; s1++, s2++);
